/** @page krb5releasenotes Release Notes

    @section krb5releasenotes_unreleased Unreleased

    - Added structured Kerberos environment checks with strict readiness
      options for service keytabs, TGTs, and default credential caches.
    - Added credential cache maintenance helpers for TGT renewal evaluation,
      optional renewal, and service-ticket prefetch workflows.
    - Added a GSS-level S4U helper that creates an impersonated client context
      from a service credential and user principal.
    - Added sandbox-aware credential cache collection redaction with
      \c accessible metadata for denied cache entries.
    - Added fail-closed handling for KDC-contacting operations when MIT
      Kerberos/GSSAPI network I/O cannot enforce an active fine-grained
      network sandbox policy.
    - Clarified cooperative cancellation semantics for MIT Kerberos/GSSAPI
      calls.
    - Clarified that @ref Qore::Krb5::GssCredential::impersonateName()
      returns a GSS credential, not a @ref Qore::Krb5::Krb5Credentials
      evidence ticket for the low-level S4U2Proxy API.
    - Expanded unit and KDC integration coverage for diagnostics, sandboxing,
      cancellation, S4U helper behavior, and credential cache maintenance.
